# svartalfaheim — the realms are PRIVATE (like the Hoard).
#
# The intent: a realm's DATA never leaves the machine, while its SCAFFOLD
# (READMEs, the secrets how-to, *.example templates) is tracked so a new operator
# can see the shape.
#
# The mechanism matters. `*` also matches DIRECTORIES, and git cannot re-include
# a file whose parent directory is excluded — so a bare `*` followed by
# `!README.md`-style exceptions silently ignores everything, and only already-
# tracked files appear to work. Re-including the directories (`!*/`) keeps them
# traversable, so the file exceptions actually take effect.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!README.md
!**/README.md
!SECRETS.md
!**/SECRETS.md
!.gitkeep
!**/.gitkeep
!*.example
!**/*.example
!*.example.md
!**/*.example.md

# Belt and braces: whatever the exceptions above, a real env file is never
# tracked. See wayof/SECRETS.md for how a company's secrets are set up.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
